# Demo dataset, curated by hand (not extracted).
#
# Seven series chosen to show the inferences of the ontology: sequel chains, layered
# classes, property chains, nominals, SWRL rules. In the Wikidata build sequelOf is
# almost empty (596 of 107,522 games), so these chains are written here.
#
# Facts checked on Wikidata (Q-ids in hasWikidataId) on 2026-11-19. For the games
# from 2010 on, the same IRIs and values as in the Wikidata build are used.
# Per game: lead developer and main publisher only, the main platforms, the genres
# that map to a genre class, release date (xsd:dateTime) and Metacritic score
# (original platform) when Wikidata has one.
#
# sequelOf is asserted only towards the direct predecessor: the rest of each chain
# comes from transitivity. The first Grand Theft Auto is left without a type on
# purpose: the reasoner types it VideoGame from the domain and range of its properties.
#
# Where Wikidata and the facts differ, the facts win and the line says so
# (GTA VI developer, Dark Souls publishers). No unique name assumption in OWL:
# companies and platforms are declared pairwise different (owl:AllDifferent), so
# the reasoner can never merge, e.g., Nintendo Switch and Nintendo Switch 2.

@prefix vg:   <http://www.videogame-ontology.org/ontology#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://www.videogame-ontology.org/ontology/abox-demo> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Video Game Ontology: demo data" ;
    rdfs:comment "Hand-curated demonstration data (seven game series), checked on Wikidata." ;
    owl:imports <http://www.videogame-ontology.org/ontology> .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Grand Theft Auto
# No rdf:type on purpose: the reasoner types it VideoGame from the domain of its own
# properties and from the range of sequelOf (GTA 2 is its sequel).

